{
  "algorithm": {
    "id": "config-v2-cross-field",
    "specification": "architecture/config/config.schema.yaml",
    "summary": "The endpoint cross-field rules stated in the schema: an entry names its key file as `<EndpointId>.key` with a derived stem, never the retired `id` (ADR-0067); unique endpoint IDs and unique aliases; a set default, an alias or an id, naming an ENABLED endpoint; static-subset peers being a subset of trust.allowed_peers; endpoint policy narrowing rather than widening profile trust (ADR-0012); and enabled advertised entries fitting directory.max_advertised. Verdict set.",
    "why_not_json_schema": "Each rule is a relationship BETWEEN fields. JSON Schema constrains shape, not agreement between two branches of a document, which is exactly the gap these vectors cover beside contracts/schemas/.",
    "wire_shape": "Endpoint policies use the shape frozen by endpoints/endpoint-config.schema.json: the bare string \"inherit_profile_trust\", or {\"static_subset\": [...]}. An earlier revision of this file used a Serde-tagged {\"policy\": ...} form that the schema never accepted — corrected as a defect, not a protocol change, since no shape ever validated both ways.",
    "test_only_ids": "Every EndpointId here is TEST-ONLY: derived from the Ed25519 key whose seed is SHA-256(\"interweave/test-only/endpoint-key/v1\\0\" || alias), tests/support's endpoint_keys, so the seed is public by construction. Regenerated under ADR-0067 decision 7 from the label-keyed entries, each label kept as the alias."
  },
  "adr": [
    "0012",
    "0026",
    "0028",
    "0030",
    "0031",
    "0067"
  ],
